    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter September 13th with a lineup optimized for high-upside speed and situational platoon advantages. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) stands as our premier play today; his matchup against Chandler features an elite 17% boost from the SP skill profile and a massive 14% platoon advantage, while his leadoff spot provides the high-volume opportunities we crave for stolen base potential. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (74.28) and **Trea Turner** (73.97) anchor the core, with **Yordan Alvarez** specifically leveraging a 0.443 xwOBA that remains too elite to fade regardless of the park factors, and **Trea Turner** benefiting from a favorable 4.69 xERA matchup that prioritizes his dual-threat skill set at the top of the order.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight our 1B and OF configurations. **Colt Keith** (69.64) is a must-start against Hughes, as his 12% boost from the SP matchup combined with the slow delivery of the opposition creates a high-probability environment for him to exploit the base paths. Our closest bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (49.89), who just missed the cut; while his SP skill projection was competitive, his lower floor and unfavorable park factors ultimately forced him to the bench in favor of the higher-rated **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.84), who carries a more reliable platoon profile against the lefty Rogers.\n\nWe must remain wary of the Catcher and Utility slots where efficiency scores have dipped. **Gary Sanchez** (41.10) faces the toughest test of the day against Burns, whose 3.42 xERA creates a significant drag on our scoring floor. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Carson Benge** (43.39), who faces a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Schlittler; while he provides value through his platoon split, the elite arm of the opposition carries an inherent risk of a zero-production day. The Zebras' success tonight hinges on these specific platoon wins and the high-leverage plate appearances from **Junior Caminero** (69.31) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.64) to maintain our category standings.",
